ation", "pts": 1, "sec": "B · Methods", "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "bare": true}, {"id": "m7u10v3Bq15", "type": "order", "prompt": "Put these in order, smallest first.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "pts": 1, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "items": ["30%", "0.15", "4/5"]}, {"id": "m7u10v3Bq16", "type": "grid", "prompt": "Is each statement always true, sometimes true or never true?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Data", "pts": 1, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "cols": ["Sometimes true", "Always true", "Never true"], "mode": "classify", "rows": [{"l": "p% of a number is less than the number"}, {"l": "200% of a number is double the number"}, {"l": "50% of a number is half of it"}]}, {"id": "m7u10v3Bq17", "type": "num", "prompt": "11 out of 28 students wear glasses. What percentage is that? Give your answer to 1 d.p.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "pts": 2, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "unit": "%", "units": ["%"]}, {"id": "m7u10v3Bq18", "type": "num", "prompt": "Find 2.5% of 200 by building it from 10%, 5% and 1%.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "pts": 1, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "bare": true}, {"id": "m7u10v3Bq19", "type": "num", "prompt": "A plant was 220 mm tall. It grew to 125% of its height. How tall is it now?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "pts": 1, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "unit": "mm", "units": ["mm"]}, {"id": "m7u10v3Bq20", "type": "num", "prompt": "Find 0.1% of 1600.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "pts": 1, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "bare": true}, {"id": "m7u10v3Bq21", "type": "explain", "prompt": "Explain why 150% of 30 is bigger than 30.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Reasoning", "pts": 2, "sec": "D · Reasoning"}, {"id": "m7u10v3Bq22", "type": "explain", "prompt": "Explain how you would compare 0.35 and 1/3.", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "pts": 2, "sec"